79 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 61 0 R
/T (Pyromaniacs play mostly from the heart, they love to close their eyes, take risks, try difficult fast phrases beyond their technical ability, play complex sounds they may not even understand theoretically. PROS: creative, spontaneous, full of energy, excitement. CONS: often loose the form, make tons of mistakes, impatience. )
/E (Pyromaniacs play mostly from the heart, they love to close their eyes, take risks, try difficult fast phrases beyond their technical ability, play complex sounds they may not even understand theoretically. PROS: creative, spontaneous, full of energy, excitement. CONS: often loose the form, make tons of mistakes, impatience. )
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
80 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 61 0 R
/T (Control-Freaks like organization, they like to play over the grid \(rhythmic accuracy\), respect the form, keep solos under control, addressing the chords properly. They like to understand what they are playing, and have a more pedagogical approach to improvisation. PROS: excellent analytical skills, good team player, can practice with more focus, overtime can grow and improve a lot. CONS: lack of spontaneity and risk taking. )
/E (Control-Freaks like organization, they like to play over the grid \(rhythmic accuracy\), respect the form, keep solos under control, addressing the chords properly. They like to understand what they are playing, and have a more pedagogical approach to improvisation. PROS: excellent analytical skills, good team player, can practice with more focus, overtime can grow and improve a lot. CONS: lack of spontaneity and risk taking. )
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [2]
>>
