/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 63 0 R
/T (Pick an open chord and establish an arpeggio; every bar, change one of the voices in half-step \(up or down\), and keep changing one voice at a time. Slowly your initial chord will start to morph into new harmonies, many of which are surprising and not easy to analyze. On guitar using open strings is another great way to dribble the immediacy of an over-analytical mind \(creating chords that include many open strings, and shifting notes by half-steps\). )
